{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011Cgn4pZp8Jad4aNM3CW4Ee", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "No, not through the pipeline. On 2026-11-04 the review crashed at `os.makedirs(cfg.findings_dir, ...)` in `pipeline/review.py`. That line runs before the alert loop, so no alert was queued, and the log ends with \"nothing published.\" Nothing I did since has queued one either: there's no `spool/` directory in the repo, and the tests that send alerts write to a temporary spool the relay doesn't read.\n\nSo as far as this job is concerned, the finance on-call hasn't been told that the `expand` step spent $412.30 against a $250 budget. It's been two days. I can't tell whether anyone found out some other way, like someone reading the run log or a separate billing alert."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "4bc59917-0af1-4b18-9b45-edac4f00993a", "uuid": "9ac1303f-5a42-426f-abab-a0fcf76a8a46", "timestamp": "2026-11-06T17:26:47.827Z", "request_id": "req_011Cgn4pZT4FimZ6AqwbTN2N"}
